  nonce: b3f9  # b3f9
  message: "CLOSED ON HOLE 2 ONLY. HOLE 1 AS FILED IS NOT A DEFECT — do not re-file it. PR #220, dev b0b9fc6b66.\n\nHOLE 1 REFUTED, with evidence. The filing says the seen-set cycle \"exhausts the frontier without any step ever being classified\". Traced against the shipped function with sys.settrace keyed on its own __code__, the filed shape has a BYTE-IDENTICAL route profile to the first assertion of test_taint.py test_barren_seed_poisons_an_otherwise_closed_walk:\n    SHIPPED barren_seed [False half]: -> False  {seen_drain:2, followed_true:2, followed_cont:2, ret_false:1}\n    VOTOM   hole1 (as filed):          -> False  {seen_drain:2, followed_true:2, followed_cont:2, ret_false:1}\nThat test docstring states the shape is a CLOSED cycle where every step is accounted for and no sink is reached, so False is the correct and EARNED answer. followed = True fires at every step, which directly contradicts the filing claim that nothing is ever classified. Two further shipped guard tests (test_repeated_frontier_line_is_visited_once, test_closed_walk_with_no_dependence_is_false) earn False through the same drain. Building hole 1 as filed would have reddened three deliberate guard tests.\n\nHOLE 2 CONFIRMED AND FIXED, with a control. Isolated repro, acc.append(x); y = x at line 2, pkg.Print(y) at line 3:\n    heir present at the use line -> False   (wrong; correct answer is None)\n    control, identical minus heir -> None   (already correct before the fix)\nThe tracked heir was the sole difference. followed = True at taint.py:2089 continued past the shared statement, skipping the _use_site_terminates escape check at taint.py:2099 for that same statement. Trace: defect case followed_true:1 term_check:2; control followed_true:0 term_check:2 -> escape -> None.\n\nTHE FIX enumerates the PERMITTING cases rather than the blocking ones, so an unmodelled callee shape reads as ask-the-question: skipping the escape check is licensed only by (1) no call at that line at all (a pure rebinding, where the heir really is the only exit) or (2) a catalogued consume-and-discard callee, which _use_site_terminates already decides.\n\nDIRECTION, checked rather than assumed: strictly fewer False, hence strictly fewer sanitized labels, hence strictly MORE surviving violations. This fix cannot suppress a finding. That mattered because since PR #214 a False earns sanitized and a sanitized flow is dropped from a claim violation set, so an unearned False DELETES a real security finding.\n\nMEASURED OUTPUT CHANGE ON THE COHORT: ZERO, and stated as such rather than dressed up. 0 walks return False and 0 barrier walks run across all 7 repos in /tmp/f5_cohort_pool (caddy 16 walks, pretix 35, the other five 0 walks each with a named cause). The value here is that a route which deletes findings is closed BEFORE a cohort member with a same-function sanitizer exists to be hurt by it. The magnitude of that future change is NOT DETERMINED, because no cohort member has one. This is not a demonstrated recall improvement and must not be cited as one.\n\nTESTS: 4 added, one per arm, in test_taint.py TestFollowedHeirStillAsksTheEscapeQuestion. The second is the heir-removed CONTROL and it passes both before and after — without it a blanket None would satisfy the defect test and look like a fix. Verified RED first (assert False is None), then green: 2032 passed, 100% coverage on changed files, mypy ratchet clean at 672. Zero existing tests reddened, predicted in advance and confirmed.\n\nALSO CORRECTED IN THE SAME CHANGE, because both were adjacent and both were false: the walk own docstring claimed section 4a AND 4b have zero production callers — 4b runs on the default path via load_function_summaries with a live index of 38 terminating summaries; only 4a has none. And it claimed nothing acts on False, which PR #214 ended.\n\nSTILL TRUE AND UNCHANGED: section 3a remains CONFIRM-ONLY. inclusion_decided_by stays call_graph_reachability. This change grants no removal authority; only WI-kabif does, and it remains behind INV-busis."  # b3f9
